{
  "_about": "Round 47 (Liam and Jonathan, 2026-11): the topics a cross-carrier question is swept for (Ask the Guides). Read by cloudflare/scripts/export_chat_outcomes.py (the checker's outcome for every program, per scope and form value -> outcomes.json) and by the Worker (cloudflare/src/chat_sweep.js: which topic, value and scope a question asks about). Patterns are case-insensitive JavaScript/Python regexes over the normalized question (chat_text.normalize: lower case, possessives and thousands commas gone). Topics and values are tried in order; the first match wins. 'form' is the form's answers (engine/form.py keys) for the value, 'base' the answers it is compared with (default: the form's defaults); 'check' is the checker topic ticked (null: only the always-on topics). 'codes' are the rules tables' Topic labels, 'rows' the pattern a row's text must match to be this value's evidence.",
